TianSemi Club Internal Use License (TCIUL) v1.0 (in inglish)

Copyright (c) 2026 TianSemi Club — INP-HB, Côte d’Ivoire. All rights reserved.

1. Definitions

"Club" means TianSemi Club — INP-HB, Côte d’Ivoire.
"Active Member" means a person currently recognised as a member of the Club by its bureau.
"Software" means the source code, documentation, assets, and files in this repository or on other storage plateforms.

2. Licence for Active Members

Subject to the Club's internal rules, the Club grants each Active Member a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable, royalty-free licence to use, copy, and modify the Software solely for TianSemi Club activities.

3. Restrictions for External Persons and Organisations

Except with prior written authorisation from the Club, no external person or organisation may copy, modify, distribute, sublicense, publish, sell, exploit, or create derivative works from the Software. Public availability of this repository does not grant any licence or permission beyond viewing it on GitHub.

4. Contributions

By submitting a contribution, an Active Member confirms that they have the right to submit it and grants the Club a perpetual, worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive right to use, reproduce, modify, distribute, and incorporate that contribution into the Software for Club activities.

5. Intellectual Property and Trademarks

All rights not expressly granted by this licence are reserved by the Club. This licence does not grant permission to use the TianSemi name, logo, or other Club marks without prior written authorisation.

6. Termination

The licence granted to an Active Member ends automatically when their membership ends or when the Club withdraws the authorisation in writing. Sections 3, 4, and 5 continue to apply after termination.

7. Disclaimer

The Software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, the Club is not liable for damages arising from use of the Software.

8. Contact

Requests for external permission must be sent to tiansemi@outlook.com.

